{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"goai-litsearch","tool":"save_to_library","arguments":{"papers_json":"[{"id":"10.1038/srep18040","title":"Ba1−xSrxZn2Si2O7 - A new family of materials with negative and very high thermal expansion","authors":["Christian Thieme","Helmar Görls","Christian Rüssel"],"year":2015,"venue":"Scientific Reports","doi":"10.1038/srep18040","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep18040","pdf_url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/srep18040.pdf","abstract":"The compound BaZn2Si2O7 shows a high coefficient of thermal expansion up to a temperature of 280 °C, then a transition to a high temperature phase is observed. This high temperature phase exhibits negative thermal expansion. If Ba(2+) is successively replaced by Sr(2+), a new phase with a structure, similar to that of the high temperature phase of BaZn2Si2O7, forms. At the composition Ba0.8Sr0.2Zn2Si2O7, this new phase is completely stabilized. The crystal structure was determined with single crystal X-ray diffraction using the composition Ba0.6Sr0.4Zn2Si2O7, which crystallizes in the orthorhombic space group Cmcm. The negative thermal expansion is a result of motions and distortions inside the crystal lattice, especially inside the chains of ZnO4 tetrahedra. Dilatometry and high temperature X-ray powder diffraction were used to verify the negative thermal expansion. Coefficients of thermal expansion partially smaller than -10·10(-6) K(-1) were measured.","citation_count":55,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref","openalex"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.jallcom.2010.10.076","title":"Synthesis and luminescent properties of Eu2+ doped BaZn2Si2O7 phosphors by combustion-assisted synthesis method","authors":["Shan-shan Yao","Li-hong Xue","You-wei Yan"],"year":2011,"venue":"Journal of Alloys and Compounds","doi":"10.1016/j.jallcom.2010.10.076","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jallcom.2010.10.076","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":10,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref","openalex"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.physb.2010.10.059","title":"Synthesis and crystal structures and luminescent properties of divalent europium-doped Ba2ZnSi2O7 and BaZn2Si2O7","authors":["Shan-shan Yao","Li-hong Xue","You-wei Yan"],"year":2011,"venue":"Physica B: Condensed Matter","doi":"10.1016/j.physb.2010.10.059","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physb.2010.10.059","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":6,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref","openalex"]},{"id":"10.1016/s0022-3697(99)00004-9","title":"Phase transition and crystal structures of BaZn2Si2O7","authors":["J.H Lin","G.X Lu","J Du","M.Z Su","C.-K Loong","J.W Richardson"],"year":1999,"venue":"Journal of Physics and Chemistry of Solids","doi":"10.1016/s0022-3697(99)00004-9","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0022-3697(99)00004-9","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":51,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref","openalex"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.ceramint.2017.10.159","title":"Effect of Al2O3 on phase formation and thermal expansion of a BaO-SrO-ZnO-SiO2 glass ceramic","authors":["Christian Thieme","Michael Kracker","Andreas Erlebach","Christian Patzig","Marek Sierka","Thomas Höche","Christian Rüssel"],"year":2018,"venue":"Ceramics International","doi":"10.1016/j.ceramint.2017.10.159","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ceramint.2017.10.159","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":7,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref","openalex"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.jallcom.2010.03.152","title":"Phase formation and properties of the LTCC composite based on the eutectic system BaO–ZnO–SiO2–B2O3","authors":["Song Chen","Shuren Zhang","Xiaohua Zhou","Ting Zhang","Ming He"],"year":2010,"venue":"Journal of Alloys and Compounds","doi":"10.1016/j.jallcom.2010.03.152","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jallcom.2010